* Week 3: {{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1994-01-29.pdf|title=Top 10 Sales in Europe|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=11|issue=5|date=29 January 1994|page=22}}
* Week 4: {{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1994-02-05.pdf|title=Top 10 Sales in Europe|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=11|issue=6|date=5 February 1994|page=24}}</ref> Germany (3 weeks),<ref name="germany"/> and Spain (1 week).<ref name="spain">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1994-04-02.pdf|title=Top 10 Sales in Europe|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=11|issue=14|date=2 April 1994|page=20|access-date=19 April 2024}}</ref> Additionally, the song was a top-10 hit also in Austria (3),<ref name="austria"/> Belgium (5),<ref name="belgium"/> France (5),<ref name="france"/> Ireland (2),<ref name="ireland"/> Italy (9),<ref name="italy">{{cite web|url=http://www.musicaedischi.it/classifiche_archivio.php|title=Classifiche|work=[[Musica e Dischi]]|language=it|access-date=29 May 2022}} Set "Tipo" on "Singoli". Then, in the "Artista" field, search "Ace Of Base".</ref> Lithuania (2),<ref name="lithuania">{{cite web|url=http://m-1.fm/top40/?topid=1247|title=M-1 Top 40|publisher=M-1.fm|access-date=6 April 2022|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150402155226/http://m-1.fm/top40/?topid=1247|date=16 January 1994|archive-date=2 April 2015}}</ref> the Netherlands (3),<ref name="netherlands"/> Norway (5),<ref name="norway"/> Scotland (2),<ref name="scotland"/> Sweden (2),<ref name="sweden"/> Switzerland (4),<ref name="switzerland"/> and the United Kingdom (2). In the latter, it peaked in its second week at UK Singles Chart on 27 February 1994. It was held off reaching the top spot by [[Mariah Carey]]'s "[[Without You (Badfinger song)#Mariah Carey version|Without You]]" (1994), and spent a total of three weeks as number two on the chart and 16 weeks within the UK Top 100.<ref>{{cite web|title=Official Singles Chart Top 100 27 February 1994 - 05 March 1994|url=https://www.officialcharts.com/charts/singles-chart/19940227/7501/|publisher=[[Official Charts Company]]|access-date=17 September 2020}}</ref> On 28 November, it entered the [[Eurochart Hot 100]] at number 29 and peaked at number two eight weeks later.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1993-11-27.pdf|title=Eurochart Hot 100|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=10|issue=48|date=27 November 1993|page=17|access-date=16 April 2024}}</ref><ref name="eurocharthot100">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1994/MM-1994-02-05.pdf|title=Eurochart Hot 100 Singles|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=11|issue=6|date=5 February 1994|page=21|access-date=15 January 2018}}</ref>

Outside Europe, "The Sign" peaked at number one in Australia (4 weeks),<ref name="australia"/> Israel (2 weeks),<ref>"The Sign" spent 2 weeks at the top of the Israeli singles chart in November 1993.
* Week 1: 16 November 1993
* Week 2: 23 November 1993</ref> New Zealand (5 weeks),<ref name="newzealand"/> Canada (5 weeks),<ref>"The Sign" spent 5 weeks at the top of the Canadian ''[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]'' singles chart in March and April 1994.
* Week 1: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=1601&app=rpm|title=RPM 100|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=|issue=|date=21 March 1994|page=}}
* Week 2: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=1606&app=rpm|title=RPM 100|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=|issue=|date=28 March 1994|page=}}
* Week 3: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=1610&app=rpm|title=RPM 100|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=|issue=|date=4 April 1994|page=}}
* Week 4: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=1613&app=rpm|title=RPM 100|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=|issue=|date=11 April 1994|page=}}
* Week 5: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=1616&app=rpm|title=RPM 100|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=|issue=|date=18 April 1994|page=}}</ref> and Zimbabwe (2 weeks).<ref name="zimbabwe">{{cite book|first= Chris |last= Kimberley |year= 2000 |title= Zimbabwe : Zimbabwe Singles Chart Book |location= Harare}}</ref> In the United States, the song [[List of Billboard Hot 100 number ones of 1994|topped]] the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] on the chart dated 12 March 1994.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/Archive-All-Music/Billboard/90s/1994/BB-1994-03-12-N.pdf|title=Hot 100 Singles Spotlight|last=McCabe|first=Kevin|magazine=Billboard|date=12 March 1994|volume=106|issue=11|page=95|access-date=14 February 2020}}</ref> This allowed Ace of Base to become the first Swedish group to simultaneously score a number one single and album on the ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' charts.<ref>{{cite magazine|title=Ace of Base: A 'Good' Sign for Sweden|last=Bronson|first=Fred|author-link=Fred Bronson|magazine=Billboard|date=2 April 1994|volume=106|issue=14|page=82}}</ref> "The Sign" also topped the US [[Cash Box Top 100 Pop Singles|''Cash Box'' Top 100]].<ref name="Cashbox"/> It was the [[Billboard Year-End Hot 100 singles of 1994|number one song of 1994]] according to ''Billboard'' magazine's year-end charts. The song was ranked at number 60 on "The Billboard Hot 100 All-Time Top Songs" for the first 55 years of the Hot 100 chart,<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/list/2155531/the-hot-100-all-time-top-songs?list_page=4|title=Hot 100 55th Anniversary: The All-Time Top 100 Songs|last=Bronson|first=Fred|magazine=Billboard|date=8 February 2013|access-date=16 January 2020}}</ref> and received a nomination for [[Grammy Award for Best Pop Performance by a Duo or Group with Vocals]] at the 1995 [[Grammy Award]]s.<ref name="grammyawards">{{cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1995-01-06-ca-17089-story.html|title=The 37th Grammy Nominations|website=[[Los Angeles Times]]|date=6 January 1995|access-date=16 January 2020}}</ref>

In 1994, ''[[Music & Media]]'' published an assessment of the chart performance of "The Sign", which stated that it "entered Border Breakers at number ten on November 21, 1993, due to crossover airplay in Central Europe. It also peaked twice at number one; on December 18, staying for five weeks and again on March 9 for a two week stay. It entered the Eurochart November 28 at 29 and peaked at two eight weeks later", and that it "[...] also holds the record for longest-running single on Border Breakers—42 weeks before slipping off on August 20."<ref>{{cite magazine|first=Karen|last=Holt|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1994/MM-1994-11-19.pdf|title=Border Breakers: Monitoring The Impact Of Euro Talent|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=11|issue=47|date=19 November 1994|pages=20–21|access-date=2 April 2018}}</ref>

